meta {
  name: 01_AcceptAndRevoke
  seq: 1
}

docs {
  Scenario: A person accepts a consent request and later revokes the consent

    Given the number of pending consent requests for the person is recorded
    When the enterprise creates a consent request for the person
    And the enterprise repeats the create call with the same id
    Then the enterprise reads the request with status Created
    And the person reads the request in the portal
    And the pending count for the person has increased
    And the request is listed for the person
    When the person accepts the request
    Then the enterprise reads the request with status Accepted
    And the Maskinporten lookup returns the consent
    And the person reads the consent
    And the consent events can be filtered by request id
    When the person revokes the consent
    Then the enterprise reads the request with status Revoked
    And the Maskinporten lookup rejects the revoked consent

  The request cannot be deleted. Revoking it is the last step and leaves it in a final
  state.
}
